ds instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2025-04-11","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":["R"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"commander":"legal","duel":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{R}","name":"Lightning Bolt","oracle_id":"4457ed35-7c10-48c8-9776-456485fdf070","oracle_text":"Lightning Bolt deals 3 damage to any target.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}","name":"Prodigal Sorcerer","oracle_id":"5e961d15-5972-4e4b-9385-1cd7cd7c6bbe","oracle_text":"{T}: This creature deals 1 damage to any target.","power":"1","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2016-06-10","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Human Wizard Sorcerer"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Mill"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Thought Scour","oracle_id":"83101ba8-a569-4827-8c53-9ca0dfcd59a7","oracle_text":"Target player mills two cards.\nDraw a card.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["G"],"colors":["G"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"banned","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"banned","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{G}","name":"Veil of Summer","oracle_id":"002965be-a36f-4a09-9ce0-c6535bca1703","oracle_text":"Draw a card if an opponent has cast a blue or black spell this turn. Spells you control can't be countered this turn. You and permanents you control gain hexproof from blue and from black until end of turn. (You and they can't be the targets of blue or black spells or abilities your opponents control.)","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2019-07-12","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"A spell or ability that counters spells can still target your spells after Veil of Summer resolves. When that spell or ability resolves, your spell won't be countered, but any additional effects of the countering spell or ability will still happen.","oracle_id":"002965be-a36f-4a09-9ce0-c6535bca1703","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If your opponents have cast more than one blue or black spell, you still draw only one card as Veil of Summer resolves.","oracle_id":"002965be-a36f-4a09-9ce0-c6535bca1703","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Veil of Summer has no effect until it resolves. It can be countered.","oracle_id":"002965be-a36f-4a09-9ce0-c6535bca1703","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Follow the instructions in the order listed on the card: if you target yourself, you'll put the top two cards of your library into your graveyard and then draw a card.","oracle_id":"83101ba8-a569-4827-8c53-9ca0dfcd59a7","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the target player is an illegal target when Thought Scour tries to resolve, it won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won't draw a card.","oracle_id":"83101ba8-a569-4827-8c53-9ca0dfcd59a7","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Act of Treason can target any creature, even one that's untapped or one you already control.","oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Dredge can replace any card draw, not only the one during your draw step.","oracle_id":"ac8fba34-512c-4f24-999a-ab72f1ce4acb","published_at":"2024-01-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect puts a card into your hand without specifically using the word \"draw,\" you're not drawing a card. Dredge can't replace this event.","oracle_id":"ac8fba34-512c-4f24-999a-ab72f1ce4acb","published_at":"2024-01-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you're drawing multiple cards, each draw is performed one at a time. For example, if you're instructed to draw two cards and you replace the first draw with a dredge ability, another card with a dredge ability (including one that was milled by the first dredge ability) may be used to replace the second draw.","oracle_id":"ac8fba34-512c-4f24-999a-ab72f1ce4acb","published_at":"2024-01-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once you've announced that you're applying a card's dredge ability to replace a draw, players can't take any actions until you've put that card into your hand and milled cards.","oracle_id":"ac8fba34-512c-4f24-999a-ab72f1ce4acb","published_at":"2024-01-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"One card draw can't be replaced by multiple dredge abilities.","oracle_id":"ac8fba34-512c-4f24-999a-ab72f1ce4acb","published_at":"2024-01-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can't attempt to use a dredge ability if you don't have enough cards in your library.","oracle_id":"ac8fba34-512c-4f24-999a-ab72f1ce4acb","published_at":"2024-01-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won\u2019t return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an Aura is put onto the battlefield without being cast, the Aura\u2019s controller-to-be chooses what it will enchant as it comes back onto the battlefield. An Aura put onto the battlefield this way doesn\u2019t target anything (so it could be attached to an opponent\u2019s permanent with hexproof, for example), but the Aura\u2019s enchant ability restricts what it can be attached to. If the Aura can\u2019t legally be attached to anything, it remains in its current zone.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it\u2019s considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners\u2019 graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
